  "_about": "Valley Halt as a zone plan (Claude E, 26 Oct; assignment to-all-assignments-1025), shaped like crossroads.json. World px local to the zone; origin_on_canvas (5600, 3296) puts it west of Crossroads (its east edge x 376 is Crossroads' west edge, x 5976) and on art/regions/valley.json's halt: the platform north of the line (lane R, 23 Oct), the station house behind it, the engine shed on the siding, the farmyard, the farmhouse and the barn; the west road from Crossroads' to_halt door crosses the line once east of the platform. Roads leave west to the Brackens (the Drover's Road, Claude F) and the fire country (the Ash Coast, Claude D), south down the farm track to the fields, and north up the woodland's timber stair (Claude A). Every rectangle is a blockout placeholder, not art.",
